<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom says no decision on Retevision.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom says no decision on Retevision.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German phone giant Deutsche Telekom AG said on Monday that it was still studying the possibility of taking a stake together with France Telecom in Spain's Retevision, but no decisions had been made.</p>
<p>&quot;We are studying an engagement in the Spanish market together with France Telecom. No decisions have been made,&quot; a DT spokesman said.</p>
<p>Retevision is Spain's second largest telecommunications network operator and is expected to be privatised next year.</p>
<p>According to a report in the French newspaper Les Echos on Monday, the French and German telecoms groups are in talks about forming a consortium to bid for Retevision with Banco Central Hispano and Spanish utility Endesa.</p>
<p>The paper said negotiations were advanced and could be concluded this week.</p>
<p>DT would not comment directly on the consortium.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097145</p>
